      "content": "it's hard to see how \"market efficiency\" helps a local shop when they're literally staring down a massive bill they can't pay. it feels like the focus is always on the theoretical benefits to the atmosphere but the actual economic damage to these communities is just treated as a side effect. don't you think the cost to small business is being massively downplayed in these discussions?",
